wb-cli (1.2.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * serial wb-scan: pass `port` to wb-device-manager as a dict with UART
    params, not a bare string — wb-device-manager silently ignored the
    string form, so `--port /dev/ttyRS485-N` scans returned 0 devices.
  * serial wb-scan: detect completion via the `scanning=true→false`
    transition wb-device-manager publishes at end-of-scan instead of
    timing out after `progress=100`. The old logic reset the wait window
    on the post-scan `progress=0` state and never declared the scan done.
  * serial wb-scan (no --port): iterate over RS-485 ports from
    /etc/wb-mqtt-serial.conf and scan each one. wb-mqtt-serial/ports/Load
    is no longer used — it returns empty when any port stanza fails
    schema validation, which silently hid bus devices. `/dev/ttyMOD*`
    (cellular modem ports) are skipped.
  * serial wb-scan: continue past per-port failures — wb-device-manager's
    `error` field is reported in `failed_ports` instead of aborting the
    whole multi-port run.

 -- Alexander Degtyarev <a.degtyarev@wirenboard.com>  Wed, 13 May 2026 04:50:00 +0300

wb-cli (1.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * serial: renamed from `modbus` — wb-cli now uses `wb-cli serial` for all
    RS-485 operations, reflecting multi-protocol support (modbus, mercury23x,
    and others). `wb-cli modbus` is removed.
  * serial wb-scan: renamed from `scan`; --slow and --bootloader modes work
    correctly — slow scan now waits for standard phase, not extended.
  * serial device-params: new command — reads configurable parameters from
    device hardware via wb-mqtt-serial/device/LoadConfig RPC (slave_id or
    string id lookup, optional --force to bypass driver cache).
  * serial device-set: new command — writes parameters to device hardware via
    wb-mqtt-serial/device/Set RPC; values are type-coerced (int/float/string).
  * serial add-devices: automatic baud-rate fixup — if a device runs at a
    different speed than the port, Modbus reg 110 is written before adding so
    no per-device baud override is stored in config.
  * serial add-devices: automatic slave_id collision resolution — physical bus
    collisions resolved via Fast Modbus by SN; config-only conflicts via
    standard Modbus reg 128 write; unresolvable cases warned and skipped.
  * serial devices: added protocol column (default: modbus).
  * modbus-fw check: added device_type column to table output.
  * lib/modbus_crc.py: shared modbus_crc16 helper extracted to avoid
    duplication between serial and other modules.
  * Tests: 53 new tests in test_serial.py covering all serial domain utilities
    and commands; 236 tests total.

 -- Alexander Degtyarev <a.degtyarev@wirenboard.com>  Wed, 13 May 2026 02:29:43 +0400

wb-cli (1.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * serial send: new command for sending raw bytes to the serial bus via
    wb-mqtt-serial port/Load RPC. No driver restart needed — request is queued
    alongside regular polling. Supports --add-crc (Modbus CRC-16), configurable
    baud/parity/stop-bits, response size and timeouts. Useful for Fast Modbus
    frames, protocol exploration, and low-level debugging.
  * modbus scan: fixed extended (Fast Modbus) scan — was reporting "standard"
    due to saw_progress bug; now correctly detects scan type from state.
  * modbus scan: added "To add to config: wb-cli modbus add-devices --port ..."
    hint after a successful scan.
  * modbus scan: improved timeout hint — mentions "wb-cli modbus ports" when
    no state received at all (driver not running / port not configured).
  * modbus add-devices: complete rewrite — three modes:
    - default: reads cached wb-device-manager state (no extra scan needed),
      filters by --port;
    - --scan-results JSON: accepts bare device list or full {data:{devices:[]}}
      envelope from wb-cli --json output;
    - --device-type + --slave-id: adds a single device directly by template
      name, no scan required.
    Required template parameters are now filled automatically from the template
    definition; missing template → warning surfaced, device still added with
    best-effort config. Duplicate slave_ids are skipped with a report.
  * modbus-fw check: added ProgressBar — shows current slave_id and port while
    checking each device; no more silent hangs on bulk checks.
  * Tests: 174 tests, all passing; new modbus tests cover scan hint, add-devices
    all three modes, duplicate skip, cached-state mode, template warnings.

