wb-cli (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: `fw_version` removed from `wb-cli info` and `wb-cli audit` JSON
    output. The field was a factory build timestamp from /etc/wb-fw-version and
    did not reflect current package state — agents misread it as firmware age.
    `release_name` (e.g. wb-2602) remains and correctly reflects current release.
  * Skills: mDNS discovery fixed — WB announces _workstation._tcp, not
    _wirenboard._tcp. Updated avahi-browse command.
  * Skills: SSH auth order — always try BatchMode=yes (key) first, then
    sshpass -p wirenboard, never plain ssh (prevents GUI password dialogs).
  * Skills: firmware upgrade section — removed hallucinated wb-update-manager,
    replaced with standard apt-get upgrade. Link to wb-releases added.
  * Skills: release_name explained — format wb-YYMM, link to
    github.com/wirenboard/wb-releases for checking latest.
  * codestyle added as git submodule; Dependabot configured for weekly updates.
  * Contributing rules: tests required for every new command; manual
    verification on real hardware required before merge.

